architecture session-workflow-recovery
  canonical_name SessionWorkflowRecovery
  family surface
  layer native-workspace
  domain Surface / Source-backed workflow recovery
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can a reviewed historical workflow become editable work in the current account while retaining exact source anchors, complete native records and an honest execution boundary?
  purpose Compile a bounded MessagePack recovery into one existing Production Studio composition and its native instruments, using the existing authenticated destination and atomic CMS record owner.
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-recovery.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-instrument-validation.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-transfer.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-view.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-recovery-view.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-destination.mjs
  source_path scripts/materialize_authored_workspace.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/workspace_recovery_mcp.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/workspace_mcp.mjs
  native_format MessagePack
  node_types RecoveryMaterial, RecoverySource, NativeInstrument, ReviewedRecovery, RecoveryOrigin
  state_types ready, retained, conflict, created, recovered, paused, stopped
  internal_calculus deterministic identity from the explicit recovery key, conversation identity and sorted source message anchors; source material changes conflict rather than silently replacing an existing identity
  internal_calculus one through four validated child records plus their composition enter the existing expected-revision-zero native transaction, bounded by its record and complete-batch limits
  invariant imported historical text and code are inert source material; recovery does not evaluate code, install providers, create schedules or execute archived commands
  invariant original text remains in ordinary private Research records with exact body hashes and explicit session-line anchors; an index locator is never called a provider message identifier
  invariant only the selected authenticated destination supplies account ownership; caller-provided actors, namespaces, databases, credentials and endpoints are absent from the account carrier
  invariant the installed destination, ready release, Production continuation and recovery grammar profile are rechecked before writing; missing or incompatible admission is an error rather than an empty account
  invariant the compiler, instrument validator, checks evaluator, composition grammar, renderer and value and MessagePack codecs have exact compatibility hashes shared by the materialized editor and account carrier
  invariant a complete current readback is required after save; a lost acknowledgement can recover only all exact revision-one records, never a stale request-ledger receipt
  invariant partial, deleted, edited, unreadable or source-changed recovered work is preserved and stops the import; retained work cannot be recreated from a stale review after its closure disappears
  invariant batch recovery commits bounded whole workflows, stops on the first uncertain or conflicting workflow and retains explicit progress; it does not split one composition across independent writes
  invariant private transfer retains validated recovery provenance and existing transfer lineage; public design reuse strips source provenance and all private instrument material
  witness scripts/tests/authored-workspace-recovery.test.mjs tests deterministic source identities, admission drift, full closure readback, interrupted responses, partial and edited records, changed source and bounded batch progress
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/workspace_recovery_mcp.test.mjs tests the real compiler and account carrier against a modeled HTTP transport, including exact private source preservation, current session, profile drift and uncertain writes; this is not a live CMS witness
  witness scripts/tests/authored-workspace-transfer.test.mjs tests private material transfer and recovery provenance preservation alongside existing source lineage
  witness scripts/tests/authored-recovery-browser.test.mjs exercises the retained Production editor, reviewed recovery, Data Checks input mapping and exports in Chrome against a modeled HTTP record transport; it does not establish native gateway acceptance
  witness scripts/tests/authored-workspace-recovery-native.test.mjs is the isolated native acceptance gate for frozen editor material, served CMS and WebAddress and Auth owners, authenticated scope refusal, lost acknowledgement and edited-record conflicts; local pure and browser tests do not establish this gate has passed
  known_gap historical procedures without a native execution owner remain source-editable drafts; recovering a detailed plan does not make its actions executable
  known_gap account attachment requires a compatible installed editor and authenticated native import; local files or passing tests do not establish that a customer profile was updated
  known_gap the archive index and reviewed private recovery packets are preparation artifacts, not a new product registry or an automatic transcript execution service
  forbidden_inference an imported or retained workflow -> completed work, current provider permission, production customer inputs, a proven external integration or live customer verification
  forbidden_inference a large historical template or persona catalogue -> that many distinct implemented workflows
  interacts session-recovery-uses-account-workspace
  interacts session-recovery-composes-data-checks

architecture authored-data-checks
  canonical_name AuthoredDataChecks
  family surface
  layer native-instrument
  domain Surface / Deterministic source-table checks
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Which exact supplied rows satisfy an authored finite contract, which fail, and which remain unresolved because inputs or an execution owner are missing?
  purpose Add a reusable Data Checks instrument to the existing Production Studio so recovered machine contracts can accept current inputs, evaluate supported checks, export evidence and reopen the same retained native work.
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-data-checks.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-data-checks-view.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-instrument-validation.mjs
  source_path scripts/materialize_authored_workspace.mjs
  native_format MessagePack
  node_types DataChecksContract, Entity, Field, Relation, Predicate, Closure, RetainedTable, ResultRow
  state_types needs_input, pass, fail, unresolved
  internal_calculus bounded scalar and exact-integer predicates, explicit UTC date tolerance, membership, requirements and interval non-overlap over exact mapped source rows
  internal_calculus exact-key and declared cross relations retain candidate row identities; latent-only matches and unsupported branches remain unresolved rather than receiving invented similarity scores
  invariant contracts are closed literal data with bounded fields, tables, source bytes, candidate pairs and result rows; arbitrary scripts and unknown operations are rejected
  invariant tables retain the actual CSV or row material, source SHA-256, mapping and example flag; changing source or configuration invalidates prior results
  invariant empty or missing tables produce needs_input with no completed output; empty input cannot satisfy a workflow by vacuous success
  invariant large integer text retains exact arithmetic and mapped-row hashes preserve signed zero; unsupported numeric conversions fail explicitly
  invariant output rows retain source hashes, exact row references and predicate outcomes; exported reports verify their result digest before materialization
  invariant declarations about provider calls, budgets, compression, publication, WAV generation or ERP commands remain declarations unless their native execution owner is separately bound
  invariant recovered contracts begin with empty production inputs; historical synthetic examples are not customer data and are never silently loaded
  invariant a new reusable design is valid empty work; public design material excludes contracts, input tables, reports and source provenance
  witness scripts/tests/authored-data-checks.test.mjs exercises the five recovered contracts, exact success and failure rows, missing inputs, latent and hybrid unresolved branches, malformed table identities, large integer timing and explicit date tolerance
  witness scripts/tests/authored-recovery-browser.test.mjs exercises real input mapping, retained input editing, evaluation, report and draft export and native-format reopen against a modeled record transport
  known_gap latent semantic matching, provider execution and historical materialization steps are not implemented by this local table-checking instrument
  known_gap the archived audio contract uses cross pairing without an exact media-hash join and applies an unconditional gain-range predicate; recovery retains these source defects visibly rather than silently correcting history
  forbidden_inference a passing table predicate or export -> an authorized payment, published content, sent follow-up, applied audio edit, ERP write, verified financial statement or live deployment

interaction session-recovery-uses-account-workspace
  source session-workflow-recovery
  destination account-workspace-mcp
  relation reviewed-native-record-creation
  preserves current authenticated session and destination admission, exact installed release, source lineage, complete native record material, revision checks and current save readback
  drops caller-inferred identities, independent storage, archived execution authority, implicit effects and stale receipts presented as current success
  invalidates_on account access, installed release, recovery grammar profile, exact reviewed source or any child record revision changing
  forbidden_inference a successful recovery transport -> a completed historical workflow or permission beyond the admitted native destination
  binding integrations/mcp/workspace_recovery_mcp.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-recovery.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/workspace_recovery_mcp.test.mjs

interaction session-recovery-composes-data-checks
  source session-workflow-recovery
  destination authored-data-checks
  relation source-contract-to-editable-native-instrument
  preserves exact authored entity and predicate declarations, source corrections, empty initial production inputs, actual input hashes and unsupported-operation status
  drops executing archived source code, loading synthetic fixtures as customer data and replacing missing model or provider owners with heuristic success
  invalidates_on contract, source table, field mapping, evaluator or native instrument revision changes
  forbidden_inference an available Data Checks pane -> end-to-end execution of every materialization or external operation described by its source
  binding cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-recovery.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-data-checks.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/authored-data-checks.test.mjs
